    <sys:String x:Key="T.Help.AutoLock">When the phone moves beyond the leaving distance, the screen locks after the configured delay.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="T.Help.AutoUnlock">When the phone comes back within range, the screen unlocks after the configured delay (local unlock must be enabled first).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="T.Help.AutoStart">Launch in the background automatically after Windows starts.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="T.Help.ManualLock">On: after you lock manually with Win+L, the app will not unlock for you again. Recommended.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="T.Help.ManualUnlock">On: after you unlock by typing your password, the app will not keep re-locking while you stay put.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="T.Help.IdleOnly">Only auto-lock when there has been no keyboard or mouse activity for a while, so you are never interrupted while typing.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="T.Help.LockWhenSeen">Used together with "Respect manual unlock": once Bluetooth was seen nearby, a later disconnect still locks the screen.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="T.Help.LockDelay">How long to wait after the device is considered away before actually locking. A small buffer avoids locking when you just walk past.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="T.Help.IdleSeconds">No keyboard or mouse input for this many seconds counts as idle. Only used when "Lock only when idle" is on.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="T.Help.UnlockDelay">How long to wait after the phone enters range before unlocking. 1-3 s works well; too small may trigger by accident.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="T.Help.ActionWarn">Show a countdown on screen before locking or unlocking. Set 0 to disable the notice.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="T.Help.RssiThreshold">Signal level required to count as "nearby"; closer to 0 means it must be closer. Sitting at the desk it is about -20 to -35, so -70 is loose. Try -55 for stricter.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="T.Help.Hysteresis">Two numbers: the first is hysteresis - the signal must drop this much more before it counts as away, preventing lock/unlock flapping at the edge; the second is how many seconds of silence counts as away.</sys:String>

